# Trading and Positions (AMM)

> Enter and sell options against the AMM

Markets created with `TradingModel.AMM` (0) trade against an automated market maker. You buy shares with `buildEnterOptionTx` and sell them with `buildSellOptionTx`; the read helpers `getEntryShares`, `getSellProceeds`, and `getClaimableAmount` let you quote trades and positions before building anything.

Options are **1-based**, `OptionSide.Yes = 1` / `OptionSide.No = 2`, `slippage` is a whole-percent bigint (`5n` = 5%), and `deadline` is an **absolute unix timestamp in seconds** (default `now + 600` when omitted) — see [Conventions](https://rain.one/docs/For-Developers/Rain-SDK/Conventions.md).

## Buying: buildEnterOptionTx

```typescript title="signature.ts" theme={null}
buildEnterOptionTx(
  params: EnterOptionTxParams & { walletAddress: `0x${string}` }
): Promise<RawTransaction[]>
```

This builder is **async** because it does real work before encoding: it reads the market's base token, checks `walletAddress`'s allowance (prepending an approval transaction if needed), and — unless you pass `minSharesOut` yourself — calls `getEntryShares` on-chain and applies `slippageTolerance` to compute slippage protection.

```typescript title="enter-option.ts" theme={null}
import { OptionSide } from 'rain-sdk-v2';

const txs = await rain.buildEnterOptionTx({
  marketContractAddress: '0xMarket',
  selectedOption: 1n,            // 1-based option index
  optionSide: OptionSide.Yes,    // Yes = 1, No = 2
  buyAmountInWei: 5_000_000n,    // 5 USDT (6 decimals)
  walletAddress: '0xYourWallet',
  slippageTolerance: 5n,         // optional, default 5%
  deadline: BigInt(Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) + 600), // optional — absolute unix timestamp; omit for the now+600s default
});

// txs = [approveTx?, enterOptionTx] — send in order
```

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
| - | - | - | - |
| `marketContractAddress` | `` `0x${string}` `` | Yes | Market contract address. |
| `selectedOption` | `bigint` | Yes | Option index, 1-based. |
| `optionSide` | `OptionSide` | Yes | `Yes` (1) or `No` (2). |
| `buyAmountInWei` | `bigint` | Yes | Spend amount in base-token wei. |
| `walletAddress` | `` `0x${string}` `` | Yes | Buyer's address, used for the allowance check. |
| `minSharesOut` | `bigint` | No | Minimum shares to accept. Auto-computed from `getEntryShares` + `slippageTolerance` when omitted. |
| `slippageTolerance` | `bigint` | No | Whole-number percent (`5n` = 5%). Default 5%. |
| `deadline` | `bigint` | No | Absolute unix timestamp in seconds. Defaults to `now + 600` (10 minutes) when omitted. A duration like `600n` reverts with `DeadlineExpired`. |

## Selling: buildSellOptionTx

```typescript title="signature.ts" theme={null}
buildSellOptionTx(params: SellOptionTxParams): RawTransaction
```

`buildSellOptionTx` is **synchronous** — it returns a single `RawTransaction`, not a Promise, and needs no `await`. No approval is required either (you are selling shares, not spending tokens).

> [!NOTE]
>
> On-chain, selling encodes the market contract's `sellOption` function — there is no `exitOption` function. The corresponding real-time event, however, is named `exit-option` (`onExitOption`), so a sell you build here surfaces as an exit-option event on the socket. See [Real-time events](https://rain.one/docs/For-Developers/Rain-SDK/WebSockets-and-Live-Data.md#pool-scoped-events).

Because the builder is synchronous, it cannot quote the AMM for you. Compute your own floor with [`getSellProceeds`](#getsellproceeds) and pass it as `minAmountOut`:

```typescript title="sell-option.ts" theme={null}
import { OptionSide } from 'rain-sdk-v2';

const quote = await rain.getSellProceeds({
  marketContractAddress: '0xMarket',
  option: 1n,
  optionSide: OptionSide.Yes,   // Yes = 1, No = 2
  shares: 1_000_000n,
});

const tx = rain.buildSellOptionTx({   // no await — synchronous
  marketContractAddress: '0xMarket',
  selectedOption: 1n,
  optionSide: OptionSide.Yes,
  sharesAmount: 1_000_000n,
  minAmountOut: (quote.proceeds * 95n) / 100n,  // 5% slippage floor
  deadline: BigInt(Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) + 600), // absolute unix timestamp
});
```

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
| - | - | - | - |
| `marketContractAddress` | `` `0x${string}` `` | Yes | Market contract address. |
| `selectedOption` | `bigint` | Yes | Option index, 1-based. |
| `optionSide` | `OptionSide` | Yes | `Yes` (1) or `No` (2). |
| `sharesAmount` | `bigint` | Yes | Shares to sell (see `getUserOptionShares` for your balance). |
| `minAmountOut` | `bigint` | No | Minimum base tokens to accept — recommended, since the sync builder computes no slippage protection for you. |
| `deadline` | `bigint` | No | Absolute unix timestamp in seconds. Defaults to `now + 600` when omitted. |

## Read helpers

All three are on-chain reads (no `accessToken` needed) and return plain values, not the REST `ApiResponse` envelope.

### getEntryShares

Quotes how many shares a buy of `amount` base-token wei would return.

```typescript title="get-entry-shares.ts" theme={null}
import { OptionSide } from 'rain-sdk-v2';

const quote = await rain.getEntryShares({
  marketContractAddress: '0xMarket',
  option: 1n,
  optionSide: OptionSide.Yes,   // Yes = 1, No = 2
  amount: 5_000_000n,           // base-token wei
});
// => { returnedShares: bigint, expectedReward: bigint }
```

`buildEnterOptionTx` uses this same call internally to derive `minSharesOut`.

### getSellProceeds

Quotes the base-token proceeds for selling `shares`.

```typescript title="get-sell-proceeds.ts" theme={null}
import { OptionSide } from 'rain-sdk-v2';

const quote = await rain.getSellProceeds({
  marketContractAddress: '0xMarket',
  option: 1n,
  optionSide: OptionSide.Yes,
  shares: 1_000_000n,
});
```

Example — selling 1.0 shares (6-decimal market) quoted 0.475 USDT:

```typescript title="response.ts" theme={null}
{
  proceeds: 475000n,
  sharesSold: 1000000n
}
```

### getClaimableAmount

Returns the base-token amount a user can claim from a resolved option (`0n` when there is nothing to claim — shown below).

```typescript title="get-claimable-amount.ts" theme={null}
const claimable = await rain.getClaimableAmount({
  marketContractAddress: '0xMarket',
  userAddress: '0xYourWallet',
  option: 1n,
});
// => 0n
```

Claiming itself is covered in [Claiming](https://rain.one/docs/For-Developers/Rain-SDK/Claiming.md).

## Related

* [Protocol fees](https://rain.one/docs/For-Developers/Rain-SDK/Protocol-Fees.md) — the 5% trading fee charged on every fill and who receives it.
* [Order book](https://rain.one/docs/For-Developers/Rain-SDK/Order-Book.md) — limit orders for `TradingModel.OrderBook` markets.
* [Split & merge](https://rain.one/docs/For-Developers/Rain-SDK/Split-and-Merge.md) — turn base tokens into complete Yes+No share sets and back.
* [Real-time events](https://rain.one/docs/For-Developers/Rain-SDK/WebSockets-and-Live-Data.md) — `enter-option`/`exit-option` socket channels per pool.


