        // Effects before interactions. `_firstClaimCheck` below makes external calls — most
        // notably `IQuestion.refund()` into the appeal oracle, a money-moving call into a
        // contract this pool does not control. Marking the caller claimed up front means a
        // reentrant `claim` cannot reach the payout path below.
        //
        // The settlement block itself is already covered by `optionFirstClaim`, but that is
        // incidental rather than by design, and it does not cover the caller's own payout.
        // This closes the one reentrancy vector here that does not depend on the base token
        // having a transfer hook.
        if (ds.optionClaimed[option][msg.sender]) {
            _revert(IRainPool.AlreadyClaimed.selector);
        }
        ds.optionClaimed[option][msg.sender] = true;

        if (!ds.optionFirstClaim[option]) {
            ds.optionFirstClaim[option] = true;
